      "mergeID": "5be233458ed7cd1f26ff2e76",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I have two avatars that rely on rigid bodies to control the movement of the model. One model uses a rigid body to move the head and the other one uses them for the arms. I've noticed that in at least two worlds both of those avatars have had their rigid bodies stop moving, whether that be rotation or actual movement. Both worlds are minigames: one is the murder world thats becoming popular, and the other world is one of the worlds that seems like lucioball from overwatch. I don't know what exactly causes this but I'm assuming that it's a script that some game worlds require to function properly considering that other worlds work fine.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Avatar rigid bodies don't work in certain worlds",
